            <ArticleTitle>Training pain resource nurses: changes in their knowledge and attitudes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>835-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE/OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To determine the changes in knowledge and attitudes of pain resource nurses (PRNs) as a result of an intensive pain management course.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Pre- and post-test design.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">A Veterans Administration hospital in the southeastern United States.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SAMPLE" NlmCategory="METHODS">18 RNs from multiple units where care is provided for veterans with cancer.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The PRNs were tested before and after a 32-hour intensive pain management course.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MAIN RESEARCH VARIABLES" NlmCategory="METHODS">Knowledge about pain management, attitudes toward pain management, and attitudes toward patients in pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="FINDINGS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Significant improvements were found in pain knowledge and attitudes toward patients in pain. Improvements in attitudes toward pain management approached significance.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The improvements in scores not only supported the effectiveness of the course but also provided additional evidence of the validity of the assessment instruments.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS FOR NURSING" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Courses such as this should be offered in other settings to encourage practicing nurses to provide better care to patients in pain and to serve as role models for their peers.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
